# Cell: ArcMutex · Vector[int] · ctor · no-spawn · pre-fix ICE 101 · post-fix `1`
#
# Part of the shared-var-decl class-fix fixture net (Core #11/#12). The
# push/len happen inside a bare `with v:` block — the shape that pins the
# writer-side class-fix's Move-follow-through WITHOUT tripping the fragile
# `for x in v:` iterator-invalidation shape (which pre-fix was green for the
# WRONG reason: downstream BB reshaping moved the violation out of the
# offending BB — Track E scout §"Corpus audit").

async void main():
    shared Vector[int] v = Vector[int]()
    with v:
        v.push(1)
        print(v.len())
